# Physical melee (#39, D-038, D-054): a swing of the sword in the IK hand hits, its damage from the size and the speed of
# the blade's stroke where it touched, a touch the minimum (#465; the damage scale itself is melee-damage.xrs); the
# trigger charges nothing and never starts the engine's strike while the IK hand holds the weapon.
# Runs on the test save mvp-goblin-fight (#70: a sword equipped, a goblin ahead in a corridor):
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence melee-swing -Save mvp-goblin-fight
# The swings are timed ramps of the simulated right controller (#634): 0.85 m in 120 ms - 7.1 m/s at any frame rate (a
# frame-counted 8 frames was 10.9 m/s at 90 fps and 3.3 m/s at 30), above the swing speed (2.5 m/s) and below a tracking
# jump (20 m/s). Every other move of the hand is a slow ramp, counted in frames on purpose (a busy runner only makes it
# slower - still no swing; the idle simulator never plays above 90 fps). An instant move is no option: it is a tracking
# jump only on a short frame - the set-up's 0.43 m in one 22 ms frame (45 fps, a busy runner) is 19.5 m/s, a swing
# (#349, TRAPS.md).
@sim idle
@save mvp-goblin-fight
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
@assert vr.melee.placed eq true
# A touch is the minimum (the default, set live: a cfg.ini of an earlier build may keep another value, TRAPS.md)
melee noswing min
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0

# The goblin held still 80 units ahead (the save has it walking away down the corridor), the sword level with its
# chest, the blade pointing ahead, the hand to the right - moved there slowly (0.43 m in 60 frames: under 0.7 m/s)
goblin_base_0036.setspeed 0
place goblin_base_0036 80
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
vr-sim head rot 0 -25 0
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@shot goblin-in-reach

# 1. A slow sweep through the goblin (0.85 m in 60 frames: under 1.3 m/s) is no swing: no swing hit (a touch, the
# minimum, reaches it only while it fights the player - melee-damage.xrs, #465)
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 0

# 2. A swing back through it: one hit, its damage from the size and the speed of the blade's stroke that touched
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
@mark
vr-sim @+0-120ms hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 1 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.swinging eq false
@assert vr.melee.hits eq {hits+1}
@assert vr.melee.last.target eq goblin_base_0036
@assert vr.melee.last.swing gt 0
@assert vr.melee.last.aim ge 0.1
@assert vr.melee.last.speed gt 1.5
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_0036 .*aim=\S+ speed=\S+ size=\S+ kind=(slash|thrust)
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=hit .*hits=1

# 3. The trigger held 2 s, then a swing: a hit like any other - the trigger charges nothing (#465)
@mark
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 180
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq true
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+0-120ms hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 2 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.hits eq {hits+1}
@assert vr.melee.last.swing gt 0
@assert vr.melee.last.aim ge 0.1
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 5
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq false
@nolog melee\.charge

# 6. The engine's own strike no longer starts from the trigger while the IK hand holds the weapon - also in the combat
# mode, where it used to strike without any animation (the owner's headset fight, 2026-10-10)
@mark
combat on
@until vr.weapon.combatMode eq true 5s
@frames 30
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 40
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq true
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 30
@nolog vr\.body\.armAnim.*strike
# No engine strike's hit: its melee.hit has no kind - the resting sword's own touches (the minimum, #465) have one, and
# a goblin the swings angered may strike the player (source=goblin...)
@nolog melee\.hit source=player (?!.* kind=)
combat off
@frames 30

# 7. A menu stops the swings: the inventory open, a fast sweep is no swing
ui inventory open
@until vr.melee.active eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.refused eq inventory
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
vr-sim @+0-120ms hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 30
@assert vr.melee.swings eq {swings}
ui inventory close
@until vr.melee.active eq true 5s

@shot after-hits
@assert errors eq 0
